Vendor Quote Automation Agent (D365 Sales)
One-Page Solution Overview
Objective
Enable sales teams to quickly convert vendor quote documents (PDF/Excel) into structured Quotes with Quote Lines in Dynamics 365 Sales, associated to an existing Opportunity.
The solution accelerates quote creation, reduces manual data entry, and ensures consistency across accounts—while allowing users to retain control over final sell pricing.

Proposed Approach & Architecture
We propose a hybrid agent + automation architecture that balances usability, accuracy, and scalability:
1. Intelligent Intake
•	User initiates the process from an existing Opportunity
•	Vendor quote document (PDF or Excel) is uploaded
•	System captures file and initiates processing
2. Document Extraction
•	Extract line-level details (product, description, quantity, cost) using: 
o	Structured parsing for Excel files
o	AI-based document processing for PDFs
•	Normalize extracted data into a consistent format
3. Data Normalization & Matching
•	Standardize extracted data into a reusable structure
•	Apply configurable mapping rules: 
o	Product ID / SKU matching
o	Alias or lookup-based mapping
o	Flag exceptions for user review
4. User Review & Approval
•	User reviews extracted lines in a guided interface: 
o	Validate data accuracy
o	Resolve unmatched or low-confidence items
•	Approval step ensures quality before system write
5. Quote Creation in D365 Sales
•	System creates a Quote linked to the Opportunity
•	Automatically inherits header data (Account, currency, etc.)
•	Creates Quote Lines with: 
o	Product (or write-in)
o	Description
o	Quantity
o	Cost (reference only)
•	User sets final sell pricing manually

What We Reuse vs. What We Build
Reuse (Native Platform Capabilities)
•	Dynamics 365 Sales entities: 
o	Opportunities, Quotes, Quote Lines
•	Product catalog and pricing framework
•	Power Automate for orchestration
•	AI Builder for document extraction
•	Optional Copilot/agent interface for user interaction
Build (Reusable IP)
•	Vendor quote import framework (staging + processing)
•	Configurable vendor layout & mapping logic
•	Product matching and exception handling engine
•	Review/approval interface
•	Reusable orchestration layer for quote creation
•	Deployment-ready managed solution (configurable across clients)

Proof of Concept (POC) Plan
Goal
Demonstrate end-to-end automation from vendor file → D365 Quote.
Thin Slice (Phase 1)
•	Single client
•	Single vendor format
•	Excel-based input (structured)
•	User-triggered from Opportunity
•	Basic line extraction + Quote/Quote Line creation
•	Exception summary
Expanded POC (Phase 2)
•	Add PDF document processing
•	Introduce user review screen
•	Validate second vendor/client pattern
•	Add audit logging and error handling

Key Open Questions
To move forward, we need alignment on:
1.	Cost Handling
o	Where should vendor cost be stored on the Quote Line?
o	Should it influence pricing or remain informational?
2.	Product Matching Strategy
o	Priority rules (e.g., Product ID → SKU → alias → manual)
3.	Exception Handling Approach
o	Allow incomplete lines (write-in), or require resolution before creation?
4.	Opportunity Integration Behavior
o	Create new Quote only, or reconcile with existing Opportunity products?
5.	Document Variability
o	How many vendor formats need to be supported initially?
6.	User Experience Entry Point
o	Button on Opportunity vs. embedded agent vs. upload interface

